{% comment %}
  Renders the Google Fonts used by the Test 1 / Test 2 assignment sections
  (test1-hero, test1-drop-teaser, test1-display-text, test2-product-grid).

  All four sections render this snippet; the browser only fetches the
  stylesheet once since the URL is identical every time.

  Fonts read from the Figma file, kept as-is (all are open, web-licensed
  Google Fonts, so no substitution was necessary):
  - Prata (display heading, Test 1.3)
  - Playfair Display, italic (script caption, Test 1.2)
  - Caveat (handwritten labels, Test 1.2)
  - Inter (buttons / form UI)
  - DM Mono (product card text, Test 2)
{% endcomment %}
{% # theme-check-disable RemoteAsset %}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link
  rel="stylesheet"
  href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@1,500&family=Prata&family=Caveat:wght@500;600&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"
>
{% # theme-check-enable RemoteAsset %}
